# void-harness:end

# Mission run journals, written by the runtime on every session. They belong
# with the rest of what the harness OBSERVES, under .void/local/ — but the
# runtime writes them here, and the managed block above does not cover them, so
# a plain `git add .` would commit session telemetry. Kept OUTSIDE the markers
# because `void-harness init` rewrites everything between them. Fixing this at
# the source (either the runtime writes under local/, or the shipped block
# ignores this path) is filed separately; every consumer project has the same
# uncovered path today.
.void/runs/

.gstack/
dist-singlefile/
